<title>UK: Green Belgian franc to devalue Thursday - HGCA.</title>
<headline>Green Belgian franc to devalue Thursday - HGCA.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>The green rate of the Belgian franc will be devalued in the European Union's (EU) agrimonetary grid on Thursday, the UK Home-Grown Cereals Authority (HGCA) said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>The HGCA calculated that the currency would be devalued to 39.6918 per Ecu from 39.6411.</p>
<p>The change would be triggered by the renewed strength of sterling which may enter the first of possibly five 10-day confirmation periods in the grid at the end of this month toward a possible revaluation on January 20, HGCA officials said.</p>
<p>On Thursday, the Irish punt will begin its confirmation period of up to 50 days as the average gap between the green and the market rates has exceeded the five-percent threshold at 5.268 percent in the last 10 days.</p>
<p>It faces a revaluation on January 10.</p>
<p>Green rates are used to calculate EU farm subsidies and intervention prices in national currencies.</p>
<p>-- Clelia Oziel, London Newsroom +44 171 542 8072</p>
